-- title:
--   Power map on μ_m extends to an F-automorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ and $E$ be fields with $E$ an $F$-algebra, let $m$ be a natural number with $m>0$, and let $\zeta_0\in E$ be a primitive $m$-th root of unity. Let $a$ be a natural number coprime to $m$, and assume that $\zeta_0^{a}$ is a root of the minimal polynomial of $\zeta_0$ over $F$, i.e. that evaluating $\mathrm{minpoly}_F(\zeta_0)$ at $\zeta_0^{a}$ gives $0$. Write $L=F(\{\zeta\in E:\zeta^m=1\})$ for the intermediate field of $E/F$ generated by the set of $m$-th roots of unity in $E$. The conclusion asserts the existence of an $F$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $L$ such that for every $\zeta\in L$ whose image in $E$ satisfies $\zeta^m=1$, the image of $\varphi(\zeta)$ in $E$ equals $\zeta^{a}$. Thus the $a$-th power map on the group of $m$-th roots of unity is realised by an automorphism of $L$ over $F$; no claim is made about the behaviour of $\varphi$ on elements of $L$ that are not roots of unity, nor about uniqueness.
--
--   This is the field-theoretic half of the construction of a Frobenius automorphism on a field generated by roots of unity: granted that $\zeta_0\mapsto\zeta_0^{a}$ sends a primitive $m$-th root of unity to a conjugate, the power map on $\mu_m$ comes from an element of $\mathrm{Aut}(L/F)$. It is used in the construction of the Frobenius element on $K(\mu_{q^N-1})$ over a $p$-adic field and, through that, in the production of explicit cocycles built from the cyclotomic character.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IntermediateField_exists_algEquiv_adjoin_rootsOfUnity_apply_eq_pow.lean

